          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>Which structure defines the T8 vertebral level by passing through the central te</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>Which structure defines the T8 vertebral level by passing through the central tendon of the diaphragm?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Oesophagus</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>The oesophagus pierces the diaphragm at T10 through the oesophageal hiatus in the muscular part of the diaphragm, not at T8.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Inferior vena cava</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. The IVC passes through the caval opening in the central tendon of the diaphragm at T8 — the highest of the three major diaphragmatic openings.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Descending thoracic aorta</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>The aorta passes through the aortic hiatus at T12, behind the diaphragm between the crura, not through the central tendon at T8.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Thoracic duct</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>The thoracic duct accompanies the aorta through the aortic hiatus at T12. At T10 it lies between the aorta and azygos vein, but it does not define the T8 level.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "At T8, the defining structure is the inferior vena cava passing through the central tendon of the diaphragm. Remember the three levels: IVC at T8, oesophagus at T10, aorta at T12."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "The IVC pierces the central tendon at T8 — the highest diaphragmatic opening. The hepatic veins drain into the IVC just below this point, which is clinically relevant in Budd-Chiari syndrome."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
